# 01 — When and scope

<!-- GEN: Why: simplifying at the wrong time or outside the diff mixes refactoring with behavior change and bloats review. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

<!-- GEN: Rules S1, S4 with the workspace's phase/diff notions. -->

## When

- After the phase's checks pass ({{checks_ref}}), as the simplicity pass.
- When review names a concrete unnecessary complexity in the diff.

## Not when

- Checks are red — fix behavior first.
- The code is already clear, or is about to be rewritten.
- Writing a new feature or fixing a bug — that is not simplification.

## Scope

- Only the files and lines changed in this phase: `{{diff_command}}` <!-- GEN: e.g. git diff --name-only <base> -->
- Something worth simplifying outside the diff → record it as a separate task ({{task_tracker}}), do not do it now.

